# Field Terrain Intelligence — environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real values locally. `.env` is
# git-ignored; never commit real keys. Vite only exposes variables prefixed
# with VITE_ to client code — see https://vite.dev/guide/env-and-mode.
#
# Phase 0 (Foundation) does not call any external API and needs none of
# these to run `npm run dev`. They are declared here ahead of time so each
# variable is documented at the moment its phase introduces the adapter
# that consumes it, instead of appearing unexplained later.

# --- Phase 1: Map --------------------------------------------------------
# MapTiler API key (free tier), used for the "Outdoor" and "Satellite"
# base layers. Get one at https://cloud.maptiler.com/account/keys/ — never
# commit the real value.
# VITE_MAP_TILES_API_KEY=

# Esri (ArcGIS Location Platform) API key, used for the "esri-*" base
# layers (topographic, imagery, terrain, hillshade, light/dark gray,
# navigation — src/services/map/MapLibreProvider.ts). Create a free
# developer account at https://developers.arcgis.com, then Dashboard >
# API keys > New API key, scoped to "Public app" / "No item access" with
# only the "Basemaps" privilege enabled — never a private/full-privilege
# key, since this one ships in the client bundle. Never commit the real
# value.
# VITE_ESRI_API_KEY=

# Either key (or both) may be set independently — MapPage renders an
# explicit "unavailable" state, not a broken map, if neither is set, and
# the layer picker only ever offers base layers whose vendor key is
# actually present (see src/services/map/index.ts).

# --- Phase 5: Weather ------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_WEATHER_API_KEY=

# --- Phase 4/8: Elevation / terrain data -----------------------------------
# VITE_ELEVATION_API_KEY=

# --- Phase 15: Synchronization / backend -----------------------------------
# VITE_SYNC_API_BASE_URL=
